	(text_box "BRIDGE_3V3: Schottky-isolated 220 uF hold-up, LDO, rail-collapse (4.5 V) detector"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(size 244.325 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "51254724-751f-5ac7-bedc-2978178081b1")
	)
	(text_box "BRIDGE_5V -> SS14 Schottky -> B5_HOLD (220 uF polymer tantalum + 1 uF) -> TLV75533P LDO -> BRIDGE_3V3. The diode keeps the reservoir from being drained by the sheet-13 loads when BRIDGE_5V collapses, so the\nsequencer, the UCC5350 input sides and the over-current latch keep running long enough to turn the low sides off first (§B13.5).\nHold-up [CALC, capture notes §3.4]: reservoir from >= 4.27 V down to 3.30 V at 60 mA (design estimate for sheets 12 + 13; WP-G to confirm its share) with C >= 158 uF effective: >= 2.5 ms (requirement >= 2 ms).\nBR5_OK (TLV7031): BRIDGE_5V / 2 compared with 0.683 x BRIDGE_3V3; high while BRIDGE_5V > 4.51 V nominal (falling trip 4.39-4.60 V worst case). Active-high 'OK' with power-on-reset low: a dead detector blocks every\nstart instead of hiding a collapse. 100 pF on the sense node: 5 us filter."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 244.325 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b401d376-ece6-5b32-a0ec-a86d040bb46b")
	)
	(text_box "Power-on reset RST_N (every latch) and RAIL_READY 20 ms (RDY)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.045 25.4 0)
		(size 269.22 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "abba478c-a4e3-571a-8568-dc0e45dc342e")
	)
	(text_box "TPS3840PL30: push-pull active-low RESET, VIT- 3.0 V +-1.5 % (VIT+ 3.1 V), output driven low from VDD = 0.3 V (SNVSB03E 6.5), CT open (50 us + 100-350 us start-up). RST_N clears all five latches; nothing is remembered from one rail cycle\nto the next: one sequence per rail cycle.\nRDY = RST_N delayed 20.2-24.1 ms [CALC] by 221 k / 100 nF C0G and a TLV7031 at 0.640 x BRIDGE_3V3 (MGJ2 and the sheet-13 oscillator settled, §B13.1 step 4). A separate RC is used because the TPS3840's own CT delay spreads 1.86:1 (RCT\n350-650 k), which cannot meet both '>= 20 ms' and the firmware's relay timing."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.045 31.75 0)
		(size 269.22 10.636)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "98f9bc97-4492-5ee1-a369-2519f994d3ab")
	)
	(text_box "Command and status inputs: 100 k pull-downs, Ioff Schmitt buffers on BRIDGE_3V3"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 579.585 25.4 0)
		(size 268.03 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "710a2237-63ee-5eeb-97e5-0396f39954bf")
	)
	(text_box "Contract §5.7: CMD_HA, CMD_LA, CMD_HB, CMD_LB, RELAY_CMD, BTEST_CMD, WIN_OPEN, TEST_MODE: 100 k to GND here and Ioff buffers on BRIDGE_3V3 (SN74LVC2G17, Ioff <= 10 uA: the main controller's 3.3 V commands cannot power BRIDGE_3V3 when the\nrail is off). OC_DET_N, IDLE_I_DET_N and (rev 0.3) IDLE_FAST_N: 100 k to GND here, so an open or unpowered sheet-13 comparator reads FAULT; buffered by inverting Schmitt gates (OC_F, IDLE_RAW, IDLE_FST high = fault, each with a pull-up).\nIDLE_ANY = IDLE_RAW OR IDLE_FST (U1269) replaces IDLE_RAW in the idle latch and the start health check (D-8). LSD_OK (rev 0.3): 100 k to GND (low = fault). K_REST_N: no pull here (pull-up on 04); rev 0.3 D-14: read through 10 k / 1 nF\n(K_REST_F, 10 us; contract issue 3 §5.7) so contact blips under about 10 us are ignored; SN74LVC2G14 gives K_AT_REST (= not K_REST_N) and K_LEFT (= K_REST_N).\nPairs share a package only where a double failure is harmless: (HA, HB) both stuck high cannot conduct without a low side; (LA, LB) are separated in time by the state machine; (WIN, TM) stuck high = test mode = patient relay blocked."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 579.585 31.75 0)
		(size 268.03 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
