	(text_box "ACT (SEQ_ACTIVE): clocked by the rising edge of CMD_LB with D = START_OK: the start is an EDGE, so a low-side command already high when the conditions become true never starts a sequence. Once set it holds itself (Q_N wired\nto its own PRE_N: a later CMD_LB edge sampling START_OK = 0, e.g. from a frozen timer, cannot clear it); only RST_N clears it: one sequence per rail cycle (§B13.3 rule 1). During reset PRE and CLR may both be low for\nnanoseconds (Q = Q_N = 1, SCES203Q function table); CLR wins as soon as Q_N rises, and nothing downstream can act in that time (RDY is low, so no high side and no lead).\nP1D (phase 1 done): clocked by LB_OFF10 (G_LB has been low 9-20 us), D = ACT. DONE: clocked by LA_OFF10 (G_LA low 9-20 us), D = P1D: set only after a phase-2 pulse really passed; if none passes, the 25 ms cap ends the\nsequence as a fault.\nFLT: set asynchronously (PRE) by any fault trigger once RDY is high; Q = fault. KON: clocked by the first K_EN rising edge, D = 1: starts the non-retriggerable coil timer.\nEach latch output has a pull toward the blocking state (ACT, P1D, P1D_N, FLT_N down; ACT_N, DONE, FLT, KON up)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 867.935 31.75 0)
		(size 253.955 17.113)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "95e4bdcc-aa1b-51c9-bb56-9216c0997fc3")
	)
	(text_box "End of sequence and fixed turn-off order: low sides at once, high sides +20 us, coil +1 ms, SEQ_HOLD +15 ms"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
