	)
	(text_box "RUN_L = NOR(DONE, FLT): goes low at the end (planned or fault) and removes both low-side enables within two gate delays (< 15 ns) - step 1 of §B13.5.\nRUN_D20 (10 k, 2.7 nF C0G, SN74LVC1G17): falls 20-36 us later [CALC] -> RUN_H low -> both high-side enables low (step 2). RUN_D1M (12 k, 100 nF C0G): 0.89-1.63 ms -> coil supply off (step 3). RUN_D15M (150 k, 100 nF C0G, TLV7031 at 0.372 x\nBRIDGE_3V3): 13.5-16.2 ms -> SEQ_HOLD low (step 4). Independent backstop: HOLDCAP_N (second threshold, 0.80, on the latched cap RC) ends SEQ_HOLD 38.4-41.7 ms after the start whatever RUN_D15M, DONE or FLT do, so a stuck end-of-sequence\nelement cannot hold BRIDGE_5V up without consent (it would also block every later sequence: one per rail cycle). Order holds at every tolerance corner: 36 us < 0.89 ms < 13.6 ms.\nEach RC charges fast through a BAS116 while RUN_L is high, so all three are ready within microseconds of power-up and never delay a start.\nOn a rail collapse the same order runs from the BRIDGE_3V3 hold-up (>= 2.5 ms): BR5_OK -> FLT -> RUN_L."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 160.496 0)
		(size 269.76 14.954)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e360c84a-ef3b-5c1b-9ace-0864afd80ef7")
	)
	(text_box "High-side enables G_HA, G_HB with the 10 us leg lockout (§B13.3 rule 2)"
