	(text_box "G_HA_P = HA AND RUN_H AND LA_OFF10 (U1222), then G_HA_I = G_HA_P AND HSK_N (U1266, rev 0.3 D-7: the high-side kill latch, group hsk). G_HA is blocked while G_LA is on and for 9-20 us after it goes off [CALC] (LA_OFF10: 10 k / 1.5 nF\nC0G charged at once through a BAS116 when G_LA rises, SN74LVC1G14). Same for G_HB against G_LB (G_HB_P, U1223, U1267). The lockouts and leads stay on G_HA_I / G_HB_I (after the kill gate), so they time what really reaches sheet 13.\nThe lockouts watch the gated enables, not the raw commands (review R-23).\nOutputs to sheet 13 through 1 k (pull-downs there). The high side may be enabled before a sequence (the 100 us lead): no current can flow without a low side."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 867.935 208.913 0)
		(size 263.23 10.636)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
