	)
	(text_box "OCI = OC_F OR IDLE_F (U1263); HSK_PRE_N = NAND(OCI, RDY) (U1264) presets the SN74LVC1G74 U1265 (D and CLK tied low, CLR_N = RST_N): HSK_N (its Q_N) falls and stays low until the next rail cycle. G_HA_I = G_HA_P AND HSK_N, G_HB_I =\nG_HB_P AND HSK_N (U1266, U1267). Path from OC_DET_N / IDLE_FAST_N to G_H*: 5 or 7 gates, <= 33 / 46 ns [CALC, SCES datasheets' 3.3 V maxima], about 47 / 60 ns with the 1 k into sheet 13's input threshold, instead of the 20-36 us RUN_D20\ndelay (bridge sim change 1: a shorted low side otherwise destroys the opposite high side). Planned ends, cap expiry, LSD_OK and rail collapse keep the low-side-first order through RUN_D20.\nDefaults: OCI pulled UP (dead OR = fault), HSK_PRE_N pulled DOWN (dead NAND = kill), HSK_N pulled DOWN (dead latch = high sides blocked), G_HA_P / G_HB_P pulled down. All of these fail to 'no high side' = no shock, found by the daily\nbridge test (F-8.3, T-8).\nSelf-test cannot set this latch (the test current, about 0.3 A, is below the 3 A and 80 A comparators): its stuck-clear failure is hidden (design §B14.5 'still hidden')."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 840.61 816.163 0)
		(size 267.185 14.954)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
