	(text_box "Phase 1: ACT (the start latch) charges 113 k thin film / 100 nF C0G +-2 %; TLV7031 U1271 against 0.6345 x BRIDGE_3V3 (57.6 k / 100 k): P1C_N falls 11.43 ms nominal after the start. P1F = NOR(P1C_N, P1D): acts only while phase 1\nis not yet latched done.\nPhase 2: latch U1272 (SN74LVC1G74, CLK = G_LA_I, D = 1, CLR_N = RST_N) sets P2S at the FIRST phase-2 enable edge, non-retriggerable; P2S charges 76.8 k / 100 nF C0G +-2 %; U1273 at 0.6345: P2C_N falls 7.77 ms nominal after the\nphase-2 start. P2F = NOR(P2C_N, DONE): acts only until the planned end.\nPCF = P1F OR P2F -> TRIG -> FLT: fault latch, normal turn-off order, BR_FAULT_N. Bands [SIM rev3-wpd/timers_rev3.cir, -20...+70 C and tolerances]: 10.93-11.92 ms and 7.44-8.10 ms; with the change order's wider spread (LR §2:\n-5.4/+4.3 %) 10.75-11.92 ms and 7.31-8.10 ms. Firmware's longest phases 10.0 ms and 6.7 ms: >= 0.6 ms margin.\nDefaults: P1C_N, P2C_N pulled down and held low by the comparators' power-on reset (= expired); P2S pulled UP (a dead latch starts the phase-2 timer at rail-up; it expires 7-14 ms later, before RDY at >= 20.7 ms, and every start\nis then refused); P1F, P2F, PCF pulled UP (dead gate = fault). RDY gates every trigger into FLT, so the power-up states cannot set a fault before the rail is ready."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 832.643 0)
		(size 259.245 19.272)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
